WEBVTT

00:00:12.763 --> 00:00:14.473
<i>When drakers arrive to a big town,</i>

00:00:15.432 --> 00:00:18.519
<i>they can finally kick back and relax.</i>

00:00:20.354 --> 00:00:21.855
<i>For just a brief moment.</i>

00:00:23.106 --> 00:00:23.941
<i>That is why</i>

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:26.652
<i>the time is irreplaceable.</i>

00:00:32.616 --> 00:00:35.827
Thank you for treating us
to dinner as well.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.331
Mika, we should get going.

00:00:42.292 --> 00:00:43.585
Hello?

00:00:46.797 --> 00:00:50.008
I'm sorry, he falls right to sleep
after drinking.

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:51.718
He's always such a slob.

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:55.931
Seems like nothing's changed.

00:00:56.223 --> 00:00:58.517
It happens when you drink
with Old Man Ula.

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:00.435
He can hold his liquor.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:02.813
Nanami.

00:01:03.438 --> 00:01:05.274
Is the Quin Zaza leaving right away?

00:01:05.649 --> 00:01:08.944
She needs repairing,
so I think it'll be a while.

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.320
I'm stuffed.

00:01:10.779 --> 00:01:12.447
Then you're lucky.

00:01:12.614 --> 00:01:14.616
You'll be here for the festival
starting in two days.

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.035
There's a festival?

00:01:19.204 --> 00:01:20.539
Did something happen?

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:25.794
What's going on? That's smoke!

00:01:26.378 --> 00:01:27.212
What?

00:01:27.671 --> 00:01:29.339
Is it a fire?

00:01:29.631 --> 00:01:30.757
That's towards the port.

00:01:30.966 --> 00:01:31.967
Mika!

00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:39.391
-Takita, let's go.
-Okay!

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:45.105
Damn it, what's going on?

00:01:45.397 --> 00:01:46.857
This is bad!

00:01:47.232 --> 00:01:48.317
It's coming this way!

00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:47.561
Damn it, we just got here.

00:03:48.395 --> 00:03:49.271
Crocco!

00:03:49.354 --> 00:03:50.230
Where are the others?

00:03:50.605 --> 00:03:52.691
They'll head here
after helping with evacuations.

00:03:52.941 --> 00:03:53.859
What about the Zaza?

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.154
You wake up Dag

00:03:57.362 --> 00:03:59.239
-and warm up the engine.
-Yes, sir.

00:03:59.406 --> 00:04:00.741
You head to the bridge.

00:04:01.032 --> 00:04:03.618
-Have us ready to launch if we need to.
-Yes, sir.

00:04:05.412 --> 00:04:08.373
So much for our shore leave.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:12.335
Now, then.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:24.931
What have you done?

00:04:25.223 --> 00:04:26.349
This is going to cost us!

00:04:26.892 --> 00:04:29.311
-Fall back!
-Run!

00:04:29.436 --> 00:04:31.438
Some people are injured!

00:04:31.855 --> 00:04:34.149
Which way are we supposed to run?

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:47.871
What's going on?!
That's your ship, isn't it?

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:50.373
You're...

00:04:53.168 --> 00:04:54.669
Come on, let me help you.

00:04:54.878 --> 00:04:55.712
Hold on.

00:04:55.796 --> 00:04:56.922
Thanks.

00:04:57.255 --> 00:04:59.800
You guys didn't kill it?

00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:01.760
No, we did.

00:05:02.344 --> 00:05:04.888
We've killed dragons of that size
plenty of times!

00:05:05.347 --> 00:05:08.642
It started moving
when we got back to the ship.

00:05:08.725 --> 00:05:09.559
What?!

00:05:09.684 --> 00:05:11.728
It means that there are dragons

00:05:12.062 --> 00:05:14.523
that are tougher than we ever imagined.

00:05:18.485 --> 00:05:20.237
We didn't give it a lethal dose?

00:05:21.279 --> 00:05:22.155
No way.

00:05:22.697 --> 00:05:24.741
-We pumped it full of poison.
-Poison?

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:31.206
We hunt with poison on our ship.

00:05:32.374 --> 00:05:35.126
We strung it up after dropping it
to the ground first.

00:05:36.253 --> 00:05:37.963
That's so barbaric!

00:05:38.421 --> 00:05:39.464
I don't care.

00:05:40.507 --> 00:05:43.552
Who cares about the details,
we need to focus on rescue first.

00:05:43.844 --> 00:05:46.555
Hurry, before the dragon attacks again!

00:05:48.223 --> 00:05:49.099
Okay!

00:05:58.066 --> 00:05:59.150
Vannie, let me!

00:06:14.291 --> 00:06:18.295
He might have been happier to die.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:20.922
When it's my time, I want Vannie to do it.

00:06:21.756 --> 00:06:23.842
We need some help over here!

00:06:25.802 --> 00:06:28.763
One, two... up!

00:06:32.642 --> 00:06:33.643
Hold on.

00:06:51.578 --> 00:06:53.538
Why is there a dragon here?

00:06:55.582 --> 00:06:57.208
And it's so...

00:06:57.918 --> 00:06:58.752
That guy...

00:06:59.711 --> 00:07:00.629
is huge!

00:07:22.233 --> 00:07:23.151
Run, Takita!

00:07:42.545 --> 00:07:43.380
Mika!

00:07:51.054 --> 00:07:52.722
It's really angry.

00:07:53.348 --> 00:07:54.182
No.

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:56.768
It's scared.

00:08:01.648 --> 00:08:03.400
Everyone get far away from here!

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:04.609
It's the town guard!

00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:07.445
Don't let it any closer to the city!

00:08:07.529 --> 00:08:08.613
You should evacuate.

00:08:08.947 --> 00:08:09.990
I'll show it!

00:08:10.824 --> 00:08:12.492
Don't just blindly shoot it, idiot!

00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:21.710
Okay! Kill it!

00:08:25.588 --> 00:08:26.506
It's working!

00:08:26.715 --> 00:08:27.716
Continue firing!

00:08:30.593 --> 00:08:31.428
Stop!

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:34.848
What the hell is that?

00:08:50.655 --> 00:08:52.323
It doesn't matter! Keep attacking!

00:08:52.991 --> 00:08:53.950
What is that?

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.495
Run! Hurry!

00:09:15.096 --> 00:09:16.139
What is that?

00:09:16.806 --> 00:09:18.558
The city is burning.

00:09:25.565 --> 00:09:27.901
-What was that?
-I don't know.

00:09:28.443 --> 00:09:29.486
What do you mean?

00:09:32.906 --> 00:09:35.283
Mika, Takita! There you are.

00:09:35.784 --> 00:09:37.452
Get the people outside the port.

00:09:38.078 --> 00:09:38.912
Gibbs!

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:41.372
-You okay?
-Yes, somehow.

00:09:41.539 --> 00:09:43.750
-We should get out of here soon, too.
-Mika.

00:09:44.417 --> 00:09:46.753
I've never seen a type like this one.

00:10:00.934 --> 00:10:02.352
Did something good happen today?

00:10:05.271 --> 00:10:06.106
Not especially.

00:10:06.523 --> 00:10:09.025
You look like you had your heart stolen.

00:10:10.151 --> 00:10:11.611
Find yourself a good man?

00:10:13.947 --> 00:10:15.240
Nothing like that.

00:10:15.949 --> 00:10:17.867
As long as you understand.

00:10:18.785 --> 00:10:20.954
Pipe dreams will ruin you.

00:10:23.331 --> 00:10:24.165
I know.

00:10:32.882 --> 00:10:33.883
What are you doing here?!

00:10:34.676 --> 00:10:36.261
We have to evacuate from here!

00:10:36.928 --> 00:10:38.763
Evacuate to where?

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:40.348
Outside the city!

00:10:40.515 --> 00:10:41.516
What happened?

00:10:42.183 --> 00:10:43.768
A dragon is on a rampage!

00:10:44.185 --> 00:10:47.814
It doesn't matter where we are
if this place gets ruined.

00:10:49.149 --> 00:10:51.776
We have nowhere else to go.

00:10:56.698 --> 00:10:59.075
What are those drakers doing?

00:10:59.492 --> 00:11:02.579
Apparently the draking ship is unusable.

00:11:03.121 --> 00:11:05.874
Honestly, first their brawl, now this.

00:11:06.499 --> 00:11:08.960
They're ruining our business.

00:11:09.377 --> 00:11:13.840
Anyway, I'm getting out of here.
You guys need to evacuate, too!

00:11:19.721 --> 00:11:22.140
So, no festival...

00:11:27.353 --> 00:11:29.063
All the merchant ships left.

00:11:29.522 --> 00:11:31.316
We should get out of here, too.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:33.234
I'm back!

00:11:34.736 --> 00:11:37.155
Takita, where have you been?

00:11:40.992 --> 00:11:42.702
Come on, time for us to evacuate, too.

00:11:43.536 --> 00:11:47.123
Then what happens to the people
who live here?

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:50.126
Well...

00:11:50.585 --> 00:11:54.047
That dragon might have stopped
moving for now...

00:11:54.214 --> 00:11:56.799
But try getting caught in its attack!

00:11:57.133 --> 00:11:59.093
Our ship will get destroyed
like the other one!

00:11:59.385 --> 00:12:02.222
You saw that heat ray and explosion,
didn't you?

00:12:02.764 --> 00:12:03.598
Yes.

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:05.308
Besides,

00:12:05.725 --> 00:12:08.603
that dragon is way too big for us.

00:12:08.895 --> 00:12:09.729
But...

00:12:10.605 --> 00:12:11.522
Gibbs!

00:12:14.651 --> 00:12:16.861
Isn't Mika with you?

00:12:18.238 --> 00:12:20.657
He was with me a second ago.

00:12:22.575 --> 00:12:24.702
What is that idiot thinking?

00:12:25.245 --> 00:12:27.914
There's only one thing
that goes through his mind.

00:12:29.207 --> 00:12:30.333
That idiot!

00:12:30.875 --> 00:12:32.669
Giraud, could you go get Mika?

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:36.214
Giraud?

00:12:39.467 --> 00:12:40.301
Gibbs.

00:12:41.177 --> 00:12:44.138
Can't we help the townspeople
onto the Quin Zaza?

00:12:46.557 --> 00:12:48.268
Load them and do what?

00:12:48.476 --> 00:12:49.310
Giraud.

00:12:49.477 --> 00:12:50.853
I understand the sentiment.

00:12:50.937 --> 00:12:54.065
Come on, we can't waste time
standing around.

00:12:59.445 --> 00:13:00.321
I...

00:13:22.635 --> 00:13:24.595
It can't fly anymore.

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:26.306
Old Man Ula.

00:13:28.975 --> 00:13:30.476
Apparently, they used poison.

00:13:31.978 --> 00:13:33.271
I can tell by the smell.

00:13:34.272 --> 00:13:36.482
It's blind as well.

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:39.736
Which is why it's afraid.

00:13:43.114 --> 00:13:44.157
Mika.

00:13:44.991 --> 00:13:47.994
Do you know what is deeper than the sky?

00:13:49.203 --> 00:13:52.415
-It's mankind's--
-I don't care about that.

00:13:54.083 --> 00:13:55.501
Is it edible?

00:13:57.962 --> 00:14:00.715
Gibbs, we need to take the townspeople
to the nearby town.

00:14:01.257 --> 00:14:04.385
We're the only ship left here!

00:14:04.802 --> 00:14:06.596
That's not realistic.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:10.058
The nearest town is still quite far.

00:14:10.808 --> 00:14:13.561
How many round trips
are we supposed to make?

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:16.564
Besides,

00:14:17.106 --> 00:14:20.693
this problem is between the city and
the ship who brought the half-dead dragon.

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:22.945
It doesn't concern us.

00:14:24.697 --> 00:14:25.823
This is not like you.

00:14:27.825 --> 00:14:29.118
Hey!

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:31.204
Mika!

00:14:31.287 --> 00:14:33.373
-Where have you--
-Hurry up and get ready!

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:35.541
That dragon is edible!

00:14:38.419 --> 00:14:39.253
Right?

00:14:40.254 --> 00:14:41.130
Lucky, right?

00:14:41.714 --> 00:14:42.548
Yes!

00:14:42.924 --> 00:14:43.925
What?!

00:14:44.675 --> 00:14:46.302
What is wrong with you?

00:14:46.386 --> 00:14:49.555
We were just talking about
getting out of here.

00:14:50.807 --> 00:14:51.641
Why?!

00:14:51.974 --> 00:14:55.103
Humans did that to the dragon.

00:14:55.853 --> 00:14:56.813
Mister!

00:14:57.271 --> 00:15:01.526
In that case, it must be humans
who put an end to it.

00:15:02.193 --> 00:15:03.945
Humans and nature must--

00:15:04.028 --> 00:15:08.533
So, we'll be able to extract the poison
from its meat and eat it, right?

00:15:11.077 --> 00:15:13.162
It also depends on the type of poison,

00:15:13.871 --> 00:15:15.581
but there are methods.

00:15:17.458 --> 00:15:20.294
We can eat that big one!

00:15:20.753 --> 00:15:22.630
Are you crazy?!

00:15:22.839 --> 00:15:23.714
Eat it?

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:31.722
I...

00:15:32.306 --> 00:15:33.182
am okay to hunt it.

00:15:34.809 --> 00:15:35.768
Vannie!

00:15:36.185 --> 00:15:37.728
A prey that size,

00:15:38.271 --> 00:15:41.732
we'd never be able
to take it down in the sky.

00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:43.860
But this is different.

00:15:44.527 --> 00:15:46.154
It's an injured dragon on the ground.

00:15:46.988 --> 00:15:49.532
Yes, we aren't responsible for this.

00:15:50.074 --> 00:15:51.868
If we fail, we aren't liable.

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:54.120
We can run if we need to.

00:15:55.788 --> 00:15:58.458
If we succeed, we get the profits.

00:15:59.167 --> 00:16:02.503
This is the only chance
a ship as poor as ours

00:16:02.587 --> 00:16:04.839
can catch a dragon that size.

00:16:07.675 --> 00:16:08.509
Vannie!

00:16:11.471 --> 00:16:15.433
Whose ship is poor?

00:16:21.731 --> 00:16:24.484
Gibbs, think of a way
to catch that dragon.

00:16:25.776 --> 00:16:26.944
For real?

00:16:27.737 --> 00:16:29.530
We're doing this, Crocco?

00:16:29.906 --> 00:16:32.283
What other choice do we have?

00:16:33.784 --> 00:16:35.119
Okay, leave it to me!

00:16:35.411 --> 00:16:38.664
We might be poor, but we have
experience and knowledge!

00:16:41.417 --> 00:16:44.462
We'll show those other crews!

00:16:45.129 --> 00:16:47.131
Time to catch a big one before our leave!

00:16:57.225 --> 00:16:58.059
Let's do this.

00:16:58.809 --> 00:17:00.311
We're drakers.

00:17:06.609 --> 00:17:08.361
I finished negotiating with their captain.

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:10.655
They'll lend us a hand, too.

00:17:11.239 --> 00:17:12.448
Here's the signed document.

00:17:12.782 --> 00:17:14.200
Was he being difficult?

00:17:14.867 --> 00:17:16.744
The captain was reasonable.

00:17:17.245 --> 00:17:19.080
His crew seemed displeased, though.

00:17:20.581 --> 00:17:21.958
Who loaded this?

00:17:22.083 --> 00:17:23.459
It was me.

00:17:24.168 --> 00:17:28.548
You have to load the ammo and gunpowder in
pairs, or they can't be used right away!

00:17:28.673 --> 00:17:29.507
Sorry.

00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:31.759
Anyway,

00:17:31.968 --> 00:17:34.804
attacking from the ground and air
at the same time?

00:17:35.179 --> 00:17:36.806
Can you even call that a plan?

00:17:37.723 --> 00:17:40.643
"Experience and knowledge" my ass!

00:17:40.726 --> 00:17:42.687
We gotta hope for the best.

00:17:42.979 --> 00:17:44.814
If it doesn't work out, we're screwed.

00:17:44.897 --> 00:17:46.816
We'll have to close up shop.

00:17:46.899 --> 00:17:48.568
As long as we're still alive.

00:17:48.651 --> 00:17:49.485
Hey!

00:17:49.944 --> 00:17:52.113
Stop flapping your mouths,
and get to work!

00:17:52.613 --> 00:17:55.616
Takita! You're loading the cannons!

00:17:56.075 --> 00:17:58.202
-Make sure you know what's in the cart!
-Yes, sir!

00:17:58.286 --> 00:17:59.120
Mika!

00:17:59.704 --> 00:18:00.997
What?

00:18:03.791 --> 00:18:04.792
Nothing!

00:18:06.669 --> 00:18:08.754
We don't know when the dragon
might lash out again!

00:18:09.171 --> 00:18:10.172
We have to hurry!

00:18:13.467 --> 00:18:15.303
Giraud seems enthusiastic.

00:18:15.386 --> 00:18:18.848
What's gotten into him?

00:18:23.227 --> 00:18:26.522
The granats are packed with double
the usual amount of explosives.

00:18:26.772 --> 00:18:29.650
It should pack quite the punch
when it explodes inside its body.

00:18:29.817 --> 00:18:30.818
Good work.

00:18:31.444 --> 00:18:33.070
I'll kill you if you miss.

00:18:34.488 --> 00:18:37.116
And we're counting on you with the ship.

00:18:37.241 --> 00:18:38.284
Leave it to me!

00:18:38.701 --> 00:18:41.120
Gibbs, we're almost finished
with the preparations.

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:42.455
We should check the plan.

00:18:57.011 --> 00:18:58.012
What's that?

00:18:59.305 --> 00:19:00.556
It's a gyrocopter!

00:19:00.765 --> 00:19:01.807
They're so rare!

00:19:01.974 --> 00:19:03.517
Are they from the other ship?

00:19:10.691 --> 00:19:13.277
What are they up to?

00:19:13.694 --> 00:19:14.528
Oh, no!

00:19:17.281 --> 00:19:20.159
Thank God this didn't get
destroyed with the ship!

00:19:20.326 --> 00:19:21.160
Yeah!

00:19:21.577 --> 00:19:23.746
That was our bounty to begin with.

00:19:23.829 --> 00:19:28.584
Our captain's crazy
for agreeing to their proposal!

00:19:28.959 --> 00:19:33.172
Yeah, we're not letting them run off
with 300 barrels of our dragon oil.

00:19:36.676 --> 00:19:38.344
We'll kill it ourselves.

00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:46.644
Did we do it?

00:19:48.354 --> 00:19:49.188
Those idiots!

00:19:49.271 --> 00:19:50.147
What have they done?

00:19:51.691 --> 00:19:52.775
It's going to attack.

00:19:53.234 --> 00:19:54.610
They ruined everything.

00:20:14.630 --> 00:20:16.215
Oh, God!

00:20:19.719 --> 00:20:20.845
No way!

00:20:34.608 --> 00:20:36.444
Those idiots jumped the gun!

00:20:37.319 --> 00:20:39.530
Go tell the others below we're starting.

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:43.534
Giraud!

00:21:04.096 --> 00:21:05.848
Please let me through!

00:21:12.188 --> 00:21:13.022
It's coming down!

00:21:17.860 --> 00:21:18.694
This is bad!

00:21:19.528 --> 00:21:21.113
This is really bad!

00:21:31.165 --> 00:21:31.999
Katja!

00:22:59.503 --> 00:23:02.006
Subtitle translation by Zensho Yamamoto
